ml_url":"https://github.com/jasonswearingen","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jasonswearingen/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jasonswearingen/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jasonswearingen/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jasonswearingen/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jasonswearingen/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jasonswearingen/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jasonswearingen/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jasonswearingen/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jasonswearingen/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2025-11-14T14:32:14Z","updated_at":"2025-11-14T14:32:14Z","body":"the issue seems system dependent.   I wonder if it's because I'm working on a \"DevDrive\"  (V:) not C:.  I'll make a repro today, and test on another system.","author_association":"NONE","pin":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3533069272/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3534829347","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/issues/112701#issuecomment-3534829347","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/112701","id":3534829347,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc7SsTcj","user":{"login":"jasonswearingen","id":814134,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjgxNDEzNA==","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/814134?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/jasonswearingen","html_url":"https://github.com/jasonswearingen","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jasonswearingen/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jasonswearingen/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jasonswearingen/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jasonswearingen/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jasonswearingen/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jasonswearingen/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jasonswearingen/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jasonswearingen/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jasonswearingen/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2025-11-14T22:05:26Z","updated_at":"2025-11-14T22:05:26Z","body":"attached is a very similar, yet not exact repro.  \n\n\n[godot-net10-probe-bug.zip](https://github.com/user-attachments/files/23556402/godot-net10-probe-bug.zip)\n\n\nit's a very simple repro with the same error, but this one I can only reproduce if referencing   something in the ModuleInitialzier.   \n\n```csharp\npublic class ModuleInitializer\n{\n\t[ModuleInitializer]\n\tpublic static void Initialize()\n\t{\n\t\tMicrosoft.Extensions.DependencyInjection.FromKeyedServicesAttribute test = new();\n\t}\n}\n```\n\n\n\n\nif I reference from my normal code it seems to work.  in my game code It fails with the same assembly load error, but from normal code.\n\nAnyway, with this repro I did track down the proximate cause:  having this in a `.csproj` file:\n\n```xml\n\t<ItemGroup>\n\t\t<FrameworkReference Include=\"Microsoft.AspNetCore.App\" />\n\t</ItemGroup>\n```\n\nhaving that, godot's not able to do the assembly probe properly.\n","author_association":"NONE","pin":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3534829347/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3534906410","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/issues/112701#issuecomment-3534906410","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/112701","id":3534906410,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc7SsmQq","user":{"login":"jasonswearingen","id":814134,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjgxNDEzNA==","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/814134?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/jasonswearingen","html_url":"https://github.com/jasonswearingen","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jasonswearingen/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jasonswearingen/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jasonswearingen/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jasonswearingen/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jasonswearingen/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jasonswearingen/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jasonswearingen/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jasonswearingen/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jasonswearingen/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2025-11-14T22:26:50Z","updated_at":"2025-11-14T22:26:50Z","body":"interestingly, when I add `Microsoft.Extensions.DependencyInjection.FromKeyedServicesAttribute test = new();` to my game's `[ModuleInitializer]` I get the OPPOSITE effect of my provided repro:  it works and my runtime `FileNotFoundException` goes away (the assembly is loaded correctly).   when I don't add that line to ModuleInitializer I need to do my `InjectGodotAssemblyResolverFix()` call for things to work.","author_association":"NONE","pin":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3534906410/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes